{:paths ["src"]
 ;; This said "src depends only on kotobase-protocol-core. The kotobase
 ;; dependency below is TEST-ONLY ... No namespace under src/ requires it —
 ;; verified by grep at the 2026-08-05 split", and both halves were wrong.
 ;;
 ;; The map said less than the prose. `:deps {}` named nothing at all, so even
 ;; the dependency the comment admitted to — core — was undeclared, and had
 ;; been since `1a74586` at 10:37 JST on 2026-08-05.
 ;;
 ;; The prose then went stale 69 minutes later. `f94b38a` (11:46 JST, same
 ;; day) re-split this repo from `kotobase-protocols`' main tip rather than
 ;; from the west pin, and that tree had already moved the store require out
 ;; of core:
 ;;
 ;;   [kotobase.protocols.store :as st]   ; core's wrapper, st/append
 ;;   -> [kotobase.store :as st]          ; the IStore protocol, st/-append
 ;;
 ;; The grep the comment cites was run against the 10:37 tree. It was true
 ;; then; the commit that carried the sentence forward is the commit that
 ;; falsified it.
 ;;
 ;; What `src/kotobase/protocols/atproto.cljk` requires, measured 2026-09-06:
 ;;
 ;;   kotobase.protocols.blocks  -> kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocol-core
 ;;   kotobase.protocols.http    -> kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocol-core
 ;;   kotobase.protocols.json    -> kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocol-core
 ;;   kotobase.store             -> kotoba-lang/kotobase
 ;;
 ;; kotobase would be needed here even without that last line: core's own
 ;; `kotobase.protocols.blocks` requires `kotobase.store`. Declaring it
 ;; directly is not redundancy — this repo names the namespace itself, and a
 ;; require you make yourself should not depend on a decision another
 ;; repository is free to change.
 ;;
 ;; Undeclared, this resolved for everyone who already had both next door and
 ;; for nobody else. The nbb line below names them by hand; a sibling checkout
 ;; under `orgs/` supplies them by accident. `kbb -M:test` did neither: it
 ;; failed at load with `Could not locate kotobase/protocols/blocks` and ran
 ;; zero tests — a red suite that reported no test result at all.
 ;;
 ;; Both pins are commits on their repository's default branch. An unmerged
 ;; SHA is a dependency that disappears when its branch does, and `deps.edn`
 ;; pins have no `verify-west-pins` to catch it (root AGENTS.md). kotobase is
 ;; held at the revision `kotobase-protocol-core` itself names, so this repo
 ;; and the layer beneath it select one revision of it rather than two.
 :deps {
        io.github.kotoba-lang/test {:local/root "../kotoba.test"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocol-core {:local/root "../kotoba.kotobaseProtocolCore"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotobase
        {:git/sha "bbf57df9dde5c1869182012860129a598382e088"}}
 ;; First-class runtime is nbb/cljs (repo-wide runtime priority):
 ;;   kbb --backend sci --classpath "src:test:../kotobase-protocol-core/src:<kotobase>/src" bin/run_tests.cljk
 :aliases
 {:test {:extra-paths ["test"]}}}
